---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'March 18, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — Kef Sensei"
  description="Terms governing use of the Kef Sensei website, service engagements, partnership arrangements, intellectual property, and data confidentiality."
>
  <section class="bg-white pt-28 pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="mb-10 pb-8 border-b border-[#E5E7EB]">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3" style="color: #E63946;">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-black text-[#111111] mb-3" style="font-family: var(--font-display);">Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#9CA3AF]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-legal">

        <p>
          These Terms of Use ("<strong>Terms</strong>") govern your access to and use of the Kef Sensei website
          located at <strong>kefsensei.com</strong> (the "<strong>Site</strong>") and any communications or
          pre-contractual interactions you have with Kef Sensei ("<strong>we</strong>", "<strong>us</strong>",
          or "<strong>our</strong>").
        </p>
        <p>
          By accessing or using this Site you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, please
          discontinue use immediately. These Terms do not replace or supersede any separate written agreement
          entered into for specific services or projects.
        </p>

        <!-- 1 -->
        <h2>1. Website Use</h2>

        <h3>1.1 Permitted Use</h3>
        <p>
          You may access and use this Site for lawful purposes only — specifically to learn about our studio,
          our work, and to contact us regarding potential engagements. Personal, non-commercial use is
          permitted. You may share links to pages on this Site.
        </p>

        <h3>1.2 Prohibited Conduct</h3>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the Site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable regulations;</li>
          <li>Transmit unsolicited commercial communications (spam) through our contact form;</li>
          <li>Attempt to probe, scan, or test the vulnerability of our systems;</li>
          <li>Introduce viruses, malware, or any other malicious code;</li>
          <li>Use automated tools (bots, crawlers) to scrape content beyond what is permitted by our <code>robots.txt</code>;</li>
          <li>Impersonate any person or entity or misrepresent your affiliation with any person or entity;</li>
          <li>Reproduce, distribute, or create derivative works of our content without prior written permission.</li>
        </ul>

        <!-- 2 -->
        <h2>2. Intellectual Property</h2>

        <h3>2.1 Our Content</h3>
        <p>
          All content on this Site — including text, graphics, logos, artwork, character illustrations, game
          screenshots, animation, and code — is the property of Kef Sensei or its licensors and is protected
          by copyright, trademark, and other intellectual property laws. Nothing on this Site grants you any
          licence to use our intellectual property except as expressly stated in these Terms.
        </p>

        <h3>2.2 Game Assets</h3>
        <p>
          Game artwork, character designs (including the "Sensei" mascot and "Roxy" character), symbol sprites,
          and other game-related assets displayed on this Site are proprietary to Kef Sensei or its clients
          and may not be reproduced, adapted, or used without explicit written consent.
        </p>

        <h3>2.3 Client Work</h3>
        <p>
          Screenshots or references to work performed under client contracts are displayed with the
          understanding that ownership of such deliverables resides with the respective client unless otherwise
          agreed in writing. Display of this work on our portfolio does not constitute a transfer or licence of
          any rights from such clients.
        </p>

        <h3>2.4 Trademarks</h3>
        <p>
          "Kef Sensei", the Kef Sensei logo, "We Master Fun", and "Roxy's Magic Reels" are trademarks or
          service marks of Kef Sensei. Third-party trademarks referenced on this Site remain the property of
          their respective owners.
        </p>

        <!-- 3 -->
        <h2>3. Contact Form Submissions &amp; Pre-Engagement Inquiries</h2>

        <h3>3.1 Nature of Inquiries</h3>
        <p>
          Submitting a message through our contact form does not create a contractual relationship, employment
          relationship, or any obligation on our part to provide services, respond by a specific time, or
          retain your submission confidentially beyond the terms described in our
          <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>3.2 Unsolicited Ideas</h3>
        <p>
          If you submit unsolicited creative ideas, suggestions, or concepts, you acknowledge that: (a) such
          submissions are non-confidential unless covered by a separately executed Non-Disclosure Agreement;
          (b) we may already be developing similar concepts independently; and (c) you will not be entitled to
          compensation if we develop something similar through independent effort.
        </p>

        <h3>3.3 No Guarantee of Engagement</h3>
        <p>
          Responding to an inquiry, requesting additional information, or providing a preliminary scope
          estimate does not constitute an offer or acceptance to enter into a project agreement. Binding
          engagements require a signed Statement of Work, Master Services Agreement, or equivalent written
          instrument.
        </p>

        <!-- 4 -->
        <h2>4. Confidentiality &amp; Partnership Data</h2>

        <h3>4.1 Our Confidentiality Commitment</h3>
        <p>
          We treat all project-specific information shared with us during the course of an engagement — including
          design documents, game concepts, technical specifications, business plans, financial projections, and
          unreleased game assets — as strictly confidential. We do not disclose client project details to third
          parties without express written consent.
        </p>

        <h3>4.2 Non-Disclosure Agreements (NDAs)</h3>
        <p>
          For sensitive projects, we are willing and accustomed to executing mutual NDAs before substantive
          discussions begin. If you require an NDA prior to sharing your project details, please request one
          at <a href="mailto:info@kefsensei.com">info@kefsensei.com</a>. Standard NDA terms cover: mutual
          confidentiality, a 3–5 year term, standard exclusions for publicly available information, and
          jurisdiction-appropriate governing law.
        </p>

        <h3>4.3 Data Security in Engagements</h3>
        <p>
          During active project engagements, we maintain appropriate technical and organisational safeguards
          to protect client data, including access controls, encrypted communications, and restricted
          distribution of sensitive materials within our team on a need-to-know basis.
        </p>

        <h3>4.4 Post-Engagement</h3>
        <p>
          Upon completion or termination of an engagement, we return or securely delete client data in
          accordance with the terms of the applicable project agreement. In the absence of a specific
          agreement, we follow our default data retention practices described in our Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <!-- 5 -->
        <h2>5. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p>
          This Site may contain links to third-party websites (e.g., game stores, partner sites, social media
          profiles). These links are provided for convenience only. We do not endorse, control, or take
          responsibility for the content, privacy practices, or terms of any third-party site. Access to
          third-party sites is at your own risk.
        </p>

        <!-- 6 -->
        <h2>6. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          This Site and all content are provided on an "<strong>as is</strong>" and "<strong>as available</strong>"
          basis without any warranties of any kind, either express or implied, including but not limited to
          implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, or non-infringement.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not warrant that the Site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of harmful components.
          We make no representations or warranties regarding the accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of
          any content on the Site.
        </p>

        <!-- 7 -->
        <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Kef Sensei and its team members shall not be
          liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising out of or
          relating to your access to or use of (or inability to use) this Site, including but not limited to
          loss of data, loss of profits, or loss of business opportunities, even if we have been advised of
          the possibility of such damages.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our total liability to you for any claim arising from use of this Site shall not exceed one hundred
          US dollars (USD $100). Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion or limitation of certain
          damages; in such cases, the above limitations apply to the maximum extent permitted by law.
        </p>

        <!-- 8 -->
        <h2>8. Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Kef Sensei and its team members from and against
          any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising
          out of or in connection with: (a) your use of or inability to use the Site; (b) your violation of
          these Terms; or (c) your violation of any third-party rights.
        </p>

        <!-- 9 -->
        <h2>9. Governing Law &amp; Dispute Resolution</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with applicable law. Any dispute arising
          under or in connection with these Terms that cannot be resolved informally shall be submitted to
          binding arbitration or, where arbitration is not available, to the competent courts of the
          jurisdiction in which we are established. You and we agree to attempt to resolve disputes informally
          by contacting us first at <a href="mailto:info@kefsensei.com">info@kefsensei.com</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Specific service agreements may specify a different governing law; in such cases, the terms of the
          signed agreement control.
        </p>

        <!-- 10 -->
        <h2>10. Modifications</h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to modify these Terms at any time. Changes become effective upon posting to
          this page with a revised "Last updated" date. Your continued use of the Site after changes are
          posted constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
        </p>

        <!-- 11 -->
        <h2>11. Severability</h2>
        <p>
          If any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable by a court of
          competent jurisdiction, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.
        </p>

        <!-- 12 -->
        <h2>12. Entire Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms (together with our Privacy Policy) constitute the entire agreement between you and Kef
          Sensei regarding your use of this Site and supersede any prior agreements or understandings relating
          to such use. They do not apply to and are not superseded by any separately executed client agreement
          or NDA.
        </p>

        <!-- 13 -->
        <h2>13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Contact us at:
        </p>
        <address>
          <strong>Kef Sensei</strong><br />
          <a href="mailto:info@kefsensei.com">info@kefsensei.com</a>
        </address>

      </div>

      <!-- Back link -->
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-[#E5E7EB]">
        <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-[#E63946] hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none">
            <path d="M13 8H3M7 4L3 8l4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          Back to home
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-legal {
    color: #374151;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .prose-legal p {
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .prose-legal h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #111111;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #F3F4F6;
  }
  .prose-legal h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111111;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .prose-legal ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem 0;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .prose-legal ul li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #E63946;
  }
  .prose-legal a {
    color: #E63946;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .prose-legal a:hover {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }
  .prose-legal address {
    font-style: normal;
    background: #F9F9F9;
    border: 1px solid #E5E7EB;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .prose-legal strong {
    color: #111111;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .prose-legal code {
    background: #F3F4F6;
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: #374151;
  }
</style>
